"""Original varied English conversations; train-candidate scenarios planned first."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns):ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','promise_vs_try',
('Tell my friend I will bring the old photographs on Sunday.','I will bring the old photographs on Sunday.'),
('Actually I have not found them yet. Say I will try, not promise.','I will try to find the old photographs and bring them on Sunday.'),
('Does that sound as if Sunday itself is uncertain? I am definitely visiting.','It leaves the photographs uncertain. To make the visit definite, you could say: “I will see you on Sunday. I will try to find the old photographs to bring along.”'),
('Use that version, but leave out old.','I will see you on Sunday. I will try to find the photographs to bring along.'),
('Which part can my friend count on from this message?','Your Sunday visit is definite; bringing the photographs is not promised.'))
add('correction','meeting_two_junes',
('June will chair our meeting in June. Can you make that less awkward?','The June meeting will be chaired by June.'),
('Still awkward. Introduce the month and the chair separately, keeping both facts.','Our meeting is scheduled for June, with June as chair.'),
('I mixed up the month. It is July, but June is still the chair.','Our meeting is scheduled for July, with June as chair.'),
('Why would replacing every June with July be wrong?','It would change the chair’s name as well as the month. Only the month was corrected.'))
add('correction','draft_not_sent',
('I drafted a message asking my landlord about the dripping tap. I have not sent it.','You have a draft ready, but the landlord has not been contacted through that message yet.'),
('Make a reminder saying follow up with landlord.','Send the message about the dripping tap to the landlord.'),
('Why did you change follow up to send?','You said the draft had not been sent. “Follow up” could imply there was already an earlier message to follow up on.'),
('I sent it just now. No reply yet.','Now a follow-up reminder would fit, since the message has been sent.'),
('Give me that reminder, without claiming the landlord ignored it.','Follow up on the message about the dripping tap.'))
add('correction','changing_review_criterion',
('Which title is clearer for a notice: “Doors” or “Use the side entrance”?','“Use the side entrance” is clearer because it tells readers what to do.'),
('Now I am choosing a title for a poem, not a notice. It is about choices.','For a poem about choices, “Doors” could work as a suggestive title. The more direct wording that helped the notice may be less useful here.'),
('So was your first answer wrong?','Not for the original task. A notice needs clear instructions; the poem has a different purpose, so the better title can change.'),
('Give me just your choice for the poem.','Doors'))
add('correction','two_mugs_one_correction',
('The blue mug is mine. The white mug belongs to my brother.','Your mug is blue; your brother’s is white.'),
('Correction: mine is green. His is still white.','Your mug is green, and your brother’s is white.'),
('The blue one belongs to our neighbour.','The blue mug belongs to your neighbour, the green one to you, and the white one to your brother.'),
('My brother has borrowed my mug today. Which colour is he using?','Green, because he is borrowing your mug.'),
('Has his own mug changed colour?','No. His own mug is still white.'))
add('correction','third_party_quote_error',
('In my notes, Tess said the hall was too small, and Ravi said the location was inconvenient.','Your notes attribute the size concern to Tess and the location concern to Ravi.'),
('I checked the recording. Tess said the location was inconvenient too. Remove the size complaint.','The corrected notes say both Tess and Ravi found the location inconvenient. The size complaint should be removed.'),
('Can I keep it as an anonymous concern?','Not based on what you have shared. Removing the mistaken attribution does not establish that anyone raised that concern.'),
('Summarise only the verified feedback from these notes.','Tess and Ravi both said the location was inconvenient.'))
add('correction','cancel_one_booking',
('I reserved a table for lunch and a separate room for an evening discussion. I need to cancel the room.','Make the cancellation specific to the evening discussion room so it does not affect the lunch reservation.'),
('Draft that. Do not give a reason.','Please cancel my room reservation for the evening discussion. Keep my lunch table reservation unchanged.'),
('The reply says both reservations cancelled. That is not what I wanted.','You can point out the mismatch and ask them to restore the lunch booking. Do not assume it has already been restored.'),
('Write the reply.','I asked to cancel only the evening discussion room. Please confirm whether you can restore my lunch table reservation.'),
('Can I tell my guests the lunch booking is definitely back?','Not yet. You have asked for it to be restored, but no confirmation has been shared.'))
add('correction','ambiguous_swap_request',
('For the display, put the bird picture on the left, the tree in the middle and the house on the right.','Left: bird. Middle: tree. Right: house.'),
('Swap those two.','Which two pictures should I swap?'),
('The bird and the house.','Left: house. Middle: tree. Right: bird.'),
('Leave the middle one alone, but make its frame black.','The tree stays in the middle with a black frame. The house is on the left and the bird is on the right.'),
('Did I ask for the tree itself to be painted black?','No. You asked for a black frame around the tree picture.'))
add('memory','missing_chapter_pages',
('My copy is missing the last page of chapter four. I have not read chapter five yet, so please avoid spoilers beyond four.','I can keep discussion within what you have read. If you share the relevant chapter-four text, I can help identify the gap without using later plot information.'),
('I only have a summary: the sisters find a sealed letter, then the page is missing.','That tells us where your reading stops, but it does not reveal what happens on the missing page. I should not invent its contents.'),
('Help me ask the library for a complete copy.','My copy is missing the last page of chapter four. Could I borrow a complete copy?'),
('Make that a spoken question rather than an email.','Do you have another copy? Mine is missing the last page of chapter four.'),
('Someone offered to explain the ending of the whole book. Is that within the limit I set?','No. You asked to avoid spoilers beyond chapter four.'),
('Would a guess about what is in the letter count as the missing text?','No. A guess would not recover the actual missing text.'),
('Which chapter have I not started?','Chapter five.'))
add('memory','tutor_student_names',
('I am organising a lesson. Amira is the tutor and Felix is the student. Felix’s mother, Mara, arranged it.','Amira will teach Felix; Mara arranged the lesson.'),
('Mara wants a short introduction she can send to both of them.','Amira, meet Felix, who will be taking the lesson. Felix, Amira will be your tutor.'),
('There is no confirmed location yet. Do not mention a classroom.','The introduction can stay as written; it names their roles without inventing a location.'),
('Mara asks if she should introduce herself as the tutor.','No. She arranged the lesson. Amira is the tutor.'),
('Who will be learning rather than teaching?','Felix.'),
('Can you draft a question asking the tutor where to meet?','Hi Amira, where should Felix meet you for the lesson?'),
('Who organised this arrangement in the first place?','Mara, Felix’s mother.'))
add('memory','picnic_silent_guest',
('At our picnic, my friend Lina wants to come but does not want to join the group games. I said that was fine.','She can attend without joining the games. The invitation should make that choice comfortable rather than treating participation as compulsory.'),
('There will be a blanket under the trees for people who just want to talk.','That gives Lina an option if she would rather sit and talk while others play.'),
('Help me write the general invitation, not a special message about her.','Come along for a picnic. There will be games if you fancy joining in, and a blanket under the trees for anyone who would rather sit and talk.'),
('I do not know which games yet. Is it okay that we did not list them?','Yes. The invitation does not need to promise particular games before you have chosen them.'),
('A friend suggests saying everyone must play the first round. Would that fit?','No. You already told Lina that she could attend without joining the games. A compulsory first round would contradict that.'),
('Should I tell everyone Lina is the reason?','You do not need to single her out. You can simply keep participation optional.'),
('Where was the quieter seating option?','On a blanket under the trees.'))
add('memory','theatre_prop_realism',
('In our school play, the letter is a prop. It should look sealed, but the actor must be able to open it without tearing it.','You need a reusable prop that looks sealed. A flap tucked in loosely could give that appearance without actually sealing the envelope.'),
('We will use that. The paper inside must stay blank because it is reused in another scene.','Use the loosely tucked flap and keep the paper blank.'),
('Write an instruction for the actor about handling it gently.','Please open the flap gently and keep the envelope and paper intact for the later scene.'),
('Can the actor pretend to read from it?','Yes. In the play, the actor can perform as though reading while the physical prop remains blank.'),
('The props helper wants to write the speech on the paper. Does that fit our plan?','No. You said the paper must stay blank because it is reused in another scene.'))
add('memory','jacket_repair_thread',
('I am repairing a button on a navy jacket. I want matching navy thread, not a contrasting colour.','Use navy thread so the repair blends with the jacket rather than standing out.'),
('The button is plain and I am keeping it.','Then the task is to reattach the existing button, not choose a replacement.'),
('Help me ask my neighbour to lend me a needle.','Could I borrow a needle to reattach a button to my jacket?'),
('Should I ask for a new button in that message?','No. You said you are keeping the existing button.'),
('They have red and navy thread. Which one matches what I wanted?','Navy thread. You wanted it to match the jacket.'),
('Add a promise to return the needle, not the thread I use.','Could I borrow a needle to reattach a button to my jacket? I will return the needle afterwards.'),
('Was a visible contrast part of the design?','No. You wanted the repair to blend in.'))
add('memory','audio_notes_no_transcript',
('I have an audio recording of a talk, but I have not uploaded it or written it out. Can you summarise the speaker’s argument?','I cannot access the recording from that description. Share a transcript, notes or the relevant excerpt, and I can help summarise what you provide.'),
('My notes say: more benches, better shade, paths kept clear. That is all I wrote down.','Your notes list three improvements: more benches, better shade and clear paths. They do not record the speaker’s reasoning.'),
('I need a heading for these notes.','Ideas for improving the public space'),
('Would “The speaker proved the park is unsafe” be supported?','No. The notes list improvements but do not establish that claim or a proof.'),
('Write a short summary that labels its source honestly.','My notes from the talk list three suggestions: add benches, improve shade and keep paths clear.'),
('I might transcribe the recording later.','A transcript could provide the reasoning and context missing from these brief notes.'),
('Have you listened to the original recording?','No. I have only seen the notes you pasted.'))
add('memory','puzzle_hint_boundary',
('I am solving a word puzzle for fun. Give hints if I ask, but do not reveal a complete answer unless I explicitly request it.','I can keep help to hints until you ask for a complete answer.'),
('The clue concerns something you use to open a locked door. Give a gentle hint.','Think of a small object that fits into a lock.'),
('Pause the puzzle. Help me tell my group I am leaving early today.','I will need to leave early today. Thanks for understanding.'),
('Make that less formal.','I need to head off early today. Thanks for understanding!'),
('Back to the puzzle: what did I ask you to hold back unless I explicitly requested it?','The complete answer. You asked for hints only unless you explicitly requested the answer.'),
('Now I explicitly want the answer.','Key.'),
('Why was it okay to give it at that point?','You explicitly requested the complete answer, which met the boundary you set.'))
add('memory','late_bus_alternative',
('If the last bus leaves before we finish rehearsal, Jo offered to drive me home. I have not arranged any other lift.','Jo is your fallback if you miss the last bus; that does not mean you have already decided to travel by car.'),
('We are hoping to finish early enough for the bus.','Then the bus remains the preferred plan, with Jo’s offer available if rehearsal runs late.'),
('Help me ask the conductor when rehearsal is likely to end.','What time do you expect rehearsal to finish? I am hoping to catch the last bus.'),
('They have not replied, so do not put an end time in my message to Jo.','Thanks for offering a lift if I miss the last bus. I do not know our finishing time yet.'),
('Rehearsal has now finished, and the last bus has gone. What was my fallback?','Jo offered to drive you home.'),
('Did I tell you that Jo had already driven me?','No. You described the offer, not a completed journey.'),
('What should I send Jo now?','We have finished, but I missed the last bus. Is your offer of a lift still okay?'))
